# Normalise line endings in the repository so a checkout is byte-identical on Windows,
# Linux and macOS.
#
# Why this file exists: BASELINE_HASHES.json records a sha256 for each of the twelve frozen
# E1-E5 files, and tests/test_frozen_files.py enforces them. Without a .gitattributes the
# working-tree bytes depend on the local core.autocrlf setting -- CRLF on this Windows box,
# LF on a Linux compute node -- so the same commit hashes differently on two machines and
# the frozen-file gate fails on one of them for no reason. The test now hashes
# EOL-canonical bytes as well, so the two mechanisms agree from both directions.
#
# eol=lf is chosen over eol=crlf because the compute machines are the ones that must not
# fail, and because LF is what git stores in the object database either way.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Binary artefacts: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.npy binary
*.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.zip binary
*.safetensors filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.bin binary
